    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "6. How to describe the temperature in Japanese\n\nAs mentioned in previous lessons, since the metric system is used in Japan, temperatures are indicated in Centigrade rather than in Fahrenheit as in the U.S. The following is a conversion table between Centigrade and Fahrenheit:\n\nFahrenheit:  23    32    41    50    68    98.6    104    212\nCentigrade:  -5    0     5     10    20    36.9    40     100\n\nConversion Formulas:\n\nTo convert Fahrenheit to Centigrade, subtract 32 from Fahrenheit and divide by 1.8:\n   Centigrade = (Fahrenheit - 32) / 1.8\n\nTo convert Centigrade to Fahrenheit, multiply Centigrade by 1.8 and add 32:\n   Fahrenheit = Centigrade x 1.8 + 32\n\nThe counter used in giving temperatures is -do 'degree,' and the pronunciation of numbers before this counter is the same as in the simple counting of numbers.\n\nExamples:\n   5 degrees    go-do\n   34 degrees   sanjuu yon-do"
    }
